ingredient_type: SINGLE_INGREDIENT
ontology_mapping:
  ontology_id: CHEBI:64736
  ontology_label: magnesium nitrate
  ontology_source: CHEBI
  mapping_quality: NARROW_MATCH
  evidence:
  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: MediaDive ingredient 1763 (CAS 13446-18-9)
    notes: MediaDive REST gives CAS 13446-18-9 = magnesium nitrate hexahydrate for
      source name 'Mg(NO3)2 x 6 H2O'. CHEBI has only the anhydrous parent (CHEBI:64736
      'magnesium nitrate'), so the hexahydrate is a narrowMatch to it, with cas:13446-18-9
      preserved as the exact-identity primary (cf. ammonium molybdate tetrahydrate).
  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: CHEBI (parent)
    notes: Parent anhydrous term CHEBI:64736 'magnesium nitrate'; no hexahydrate term
      exists in CHEBI.
  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: MIM curation (#342)
    notes: 'mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch
      -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning*
      than CHEBI:64736 (''magnesium nitrate'') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies:
      it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 ''hydrate'', never under the anhydrous compound,
      which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance
      containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims
      similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record''s own identifier
      are unchanged.'
  - evidence_type: MANUAL_CURATION
    source: MIM Step7d scientific review (#901)
    notes: 'MediaDiveingredient1763 explicitly names Mg(NO3)2 x6H2O and CAS13446-18-9;
      freshPubChemCAS resolvesCID202877 with magnesium dinitrate hexahydrate/H12MgN2O12.
      ParentCHEBI64736 is magnesium nitrate withoutwaters. No exacteligiblehydrate
      candidatefound. RetainformCAS and broadMatch toparent with B1registry; no inventedchemicalprops.
      See the complete identity, mapping, chemistry and synonym assessment in reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/authors/science-b/full-assessments.json;
      owner selector data/ingredients/mapped/Magnesium_Nitrate_Hexahydrate.yaml. Primary
      source references: https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureBotHT; https://mediadive.dsmz.de/rest/ingredients;
      https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/13446-18-9/property/MolecularFormula,MolecularWeight,InChI,InChIKey,IUPACName/JSON;
      https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/64736/. Captures, exact
      input hashes and scope limits: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json.
      This curation adds no scientific, mapping-release or role approval; changed
      owner bytes withdraw inherited support.'
  - evidence_type: LLM_SUGGESTION
    source: MIM issue1201 continuation; c-mediadive-1763,c-pubchem-13446-18-9
    notes: The flattened historical token MgNO32 x 6 H2O omits nitrate parentheses
      and does not literally encode Mg(NO3)2. The primary source names Mg(NO3)2 x
      6 H2O and CAS13446-18-9. Preserve the malformed token as REJECTED_LABEL while
      keeping the correctly parenthesized source alias and existing hexahydrate CAS
      identity.
